diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..f707fc4 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -105,3 +105,54 @@ knife ssh 'hostname:fizzy-lb-*' 'sudo docker exec fizzy-load-balancer kamal-prox
 ## License
 
 fizzy-saas is released under the [O'Saasy License](LICENSE.md).
+
+## Hosted billing
+
+Plans are defined in `Plan`: Free includes 1,000 published cards and 1 GB;
+Unlimited is $20/month with unlimited cards and 5 GB; Unlimited+ is $25/month
+with unlimited cards and 500 GB. Drafts do not consume the card allowance.
+Self-hosted installations do not load billing or enforce these limits.
+
+Configure these existing deployment secrets before enabling checkout:
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (the signing secret for this endpoint)
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` — the recurring $20/month USD price
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID` — the recurring $25/month USD price
+
+Enable Stripe's customer portal and allow switching between those two prices.
+Account admins use **Upgrade** in account settings to open Stripe Checkout, or
+**Manage billing** to open the portal. Neither return URLs nor client-supplied
+prices grant entitlements: only verified subscription events do.
+
+Register the **unprefixed** endpoint `POST /stripe/webhooks` for
+`customer.subscription.created`, `customer.subscription.updated`, and
+`customer.subscription.deleted`. The handler verifies the signature, uses the
+saved Stripe customer ID to find the account, and stores event receipts and
+subscription changes transactionally. Duplicate and older events are ignored.
+Active/trialing subscriptions receive their plan's allowances; cancellation at
+period end retains access until Stripe reports the subscription ended. Other
+statuses fall back to Free. No Stripe API calls are needed to process webhooks.
+
+Staff tools are at `/admin/accounts`. **Comp** grants Unlimited without creating
+or changing a Stripe subscription; **Uncomp** removes that grant (an existing
+paid subscription is preserved). These tools do not stop any existing Stripe
+charges. **Override** replaces the effective card count and/or bytes used; blank
+fields use measured usage, zero is valid, and **Reset** removes the override.
+Existing larger storage exceptions remain honored.
+
+The SaaS database needs the new billing migration (`bin/rails db:migrate`). For
+an offline check with SQLite:
+
+```sh
+SAAS=true DATABASE_ADAPTER=sqlite PARALLEL_WORKERS=1 bin/rails test \
+  saas/test/models/account/billing_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/account/billing_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/card/card_limited_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/admin/accounts_controller_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/stripe/webhooks_controller_test.rb
+```
+
+These tests stub Stripe's checkout/portal APIs, sign local webhook payloads, and
+disable external network connections for Stripe tests. No live credentials or
+Stripe connectivity are required.
diff --git a/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb b/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb
